    "summary": "Harp made of wood with a rectangular-faced wood sound box, rounded beneath. Skin membrane secured by cane pins. Two circular sound holes at opposing top and bottom corners. Sound box surmounted by carved wood head into which is fixed curved wood neck. Carved head decorated with brass tacks. Five peg holes; four pegs remain bound with cane strings. Two of strings are still attached to wooden string bar which is inserted into skin membrane.",
